{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "MNT-03 ownership ratchet. Every cross-module write the census measures in the shipped owner and peer pages is listed here with its writer, count and a named rationale; the census must match exactly (tests/js/test_ownership_census.cjs). migratedFeatures lists each feature state owner and the shared state it retired: any write to a retired target or directly to an owner fails. Regenerate the counts with `node tests/js/ownership_census.js --write-baseline` only after removing coupling.",
  "rationales": {
    "dom-handle": "Write to a DOM element property through another module's cached element handle (a const holding document.querySelector). The DOM is the page's shared presentation surface, not feature state; the write changes what the user sees and no JavaScript state is shared through it.",
    "single-writer": "Every write to this owner-state field is in exactly the one feature module listed; the field is declared in the shared createOwnerState bag only so other modules can read it. Not one of the six MNT-03 features. The entry pins that writer and its write count: a second writer, or more writes, fails the census.",
    "live-reconciliation": "main/events.js is the owner page's WebSocket reconciliation router: it applies daemon-pushed updates (courier media, folder progress, typing, read markers, debug entries) to state the listed feature module otherwise maintains. Two writers by design (snapshot owner plus live router); a third writer or more writes fails the census.",
    "conversation-selection": "Conversation navigation state (selected peer or group, its detail, typing indicators, device drawer) is switched by main/selection.js and main/groups.js together, and settings_save.js clears typing when the user disables it. One navigation transition spread over the modules that own each surface; not one of the six MNT-03 features.",
    "activity-feed": "Activity feed filters and events: main/activity.js owns them, main/status.js restores the saved filters at startup, and settings_storage.js clears the events when the user wipes local traces. Not one of the six MNT-03 features; the entry pins those writers.",
    "status-snapshots": "Daemon status and fabric snapshots: main/status.js refreshes them on the polling cluster, and settings_network.js refreshes them while the network settings pane is open. Two readers of the same endpoint writing the same snapshot field; not one of the six MNT-03 features.",
    "composer-staging": "Composer staging (attachments queued for one send): staged by composer_staging.js, edited by image_editor.js, consumed by composer_send.js. Three steps of one send intent; not one of the six MNT-03 features. The entry pins exactly those writers.",
    "view-toggle": "A view toggle several surfaces switch (files pane mode, discovery sheet, folder conflict summary, frame budget, peer map refresh). Each write sets the visible mode or a fresh summary; not feature state of the six MNT-03 features. The entry pins the writers.",
    "peer-function-hooks": "Deliberate one-time function-hook composition documented in frontend/peer/README.md: ui/public_api.js and ui/chat.js wrap transport and pairing functions at module load to install the pairing and chat handlers. tests/test_browser_peer_pairing_integrity.py executes these exact wrapper sections; rebinding is composition, not state.",
    "peer-pairing-session": "The peer SAS pairing session object. tests/e2e/test_peer_chat_outbox_durability.py assigns window.__oneLinkPeer.state.pairing directly, so it stays an ordinary shared field (an owned read-only field would break that public test surface). pairing/handshake.js writes it; auto_pair.js stores the daemon key for it; outbox_contract.js binds it."
  },
